                            <comment id="16503332" author="isapego" created="Wed, 6 Jun 2018 13:55:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It seems that informatica assumes that ODBC driver is thread-safe and tries to destroy connection, while another thread still sending data to a server.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16503422" author="isapego" created="Wed, 6 Jun 2018 15:09:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ok, it seems like an issue is really a &lt;tt&gt;select()&lt;/tt&gt; call with the socket handle which is larger than 1023. I&apos;m going to use &lt;tt&gt;poll()&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;instead for Linux.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
